{"step_index":829,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:27:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:27:44+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:27:44+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Walk/Basic.lean`\nTotal Lines: 522\nTotal Bytes: 19077\nShowing lines 50 to 90\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n50: walk visits is `SimpleGraph.Walk.support`.\n51: \n52: See `SimpleGraph.Walk.nil'` and `SimpleGraph.Walk.cons'` for patterns that\n53: can be useful in definitions since they make the vertices explicit. -/\n54: inductive Walk : V → V → Type u\n55:   | nil {u : V} : Walk u u\n56:   | cons {u v w : V} (h : G.Adj u v) (p : Walk v w) : Walk u w\n57:   deriving DecidableEq\n58: \n59: attribute [refl] Walk.nil\n60: \n61: @[simps]\n62: instance Walk.instInhabited (v : V) : Inhabited (G.Walk v v) := ⟨Walk.nil⟩\n63: \n64: /-- The one-edge walk associated to a pair of adjacent vertices. -/\n65: @[match_pattern, reducible]\n66: def Adj.toWalk {G : SimpleGraph V} {u v : V} (h : G.Adj u v) : G.Walk u v :=\n67:   Walk.cons h Walk.nil\n68: \n69: namespace Walk\n70: \n71: variable {G}\n72: \n73: /-- Pattern to get `Walk.nil` with the vertex as an explicit argument. -/\n74: @[match_pattern]\n75: abbrev nil' (u : V) : G.Walk u u := Walk.nil\n76: \n77: /-- Pattern to get `Walk.cons` with the vertices as explicit arguments. -/\n78: @[match_pattern]\n79: abbrev cons' (u v w : V) (h : G.Adj u v) (p : G.Walk v w) : G.Walk u w := Walk.cons h p\n80: \n81: theorem exists_eq_cons_of_ne {u v : V} (hne : u ≠ v) :\n82:     ∀ (p : G.Walk u v), ∃ (w : V) (h : G.Adj u w) (p' : G.Walk w v), p = cons h p'\n83:   | nil => (hne rfl).elim\n84:   | cons h p' =>