{"step_index":830,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:27:44Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Walk Reversal Property**\n\nExamining the `reverse` function for `Walk` structures, defined recursively. The goal is to prove `w ∈ ballWithin G p.length v` for a given walk `p`. Considering a direct induction on `p` to establish this property, starting with the base case `nil`. In the inductive step `cons h p`, it is observed that `u` is related to `v`, and `p` is a `Walk v w`, and finally noticing the use of `ballWithin G (p.length + 1) u`.\n\n\n**Verifying Set Inclusion Property**\n\nConsidered proving that if `x` is within `k` steps of `v`, and `u` is adjacent to `v`, then `x` is within `k+1` steps of `u`. This suggests that `ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + 1) u`. The definition of `ballWithin` reveals that the outer step is at the end of the walk, not the beginning, explaining the necessity of the `Walk.reverse` operation.\n\nThe core idea is, that we can prove `w` is in the ball of radius `q.length` around v, using `reverse` function. It seems induction on the reversed walk, which is a walk from `w` to `v` might lead to a formal proof. The reversed walk is used to establish the key relationship.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (k : ℕ) (v u w : V) (hu : u ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v) (hadj : G.Adj u w) :\\n    w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\\n  apply Finset.mem_union_right\\n  apply Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr\\n  refine ⟨u, hu, ?_⟩\\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter]\\n  exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩\\n\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk_to {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (v : V) : ∀ {w : V} (q : G.Walk w v), w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G q.length v\\n  | _, SimpleGraph.Walk.nil => by\\n    dsimp [SimpleGraph.Walk.length, GraphCalc.ballWithin]\\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self v\\n  | _, SimpleGraph.Walk.cons hadj q' => by\\n    dsimp [SimpleGraph.Walk.length]\\n    exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G q'.length v _ _ (mem_ballWithin_of_walk_to v q') hadj.symm\\n\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G p.length v := by\\n  have h := mem_ballWithin_of_walk_to G v p.reverse\\n  rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_reverse] at h\\n  exact h\\nEOF\\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\\n\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"20000","toolAction":"\"Checking scratch.lean with check.sh\"","toolSummary":"\"Verify walk lemmas in scratch.lean\""}}]}
{"step_index":831,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:27:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:27:50+02:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: 77001943-b7df-4df1-ba5c-db7288bf8e72/task-831\nTask Description: cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (k : ℕ) (v u w : V) (hu : u ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v) (hadj : G.Adj u w) :\n    w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n  apply Finset.mem_union_right\n  apply Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr\n  refine ⟨u, hu, ?_⟩\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n  exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk_to {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (v : V) : ∀ {w : V} (q : G.Walk w v), w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G q.length v\n  | _, SimpleGraph.Walk.nil => by\n    dsimp [SimpleGraph.Walk.length, GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self v\n  | _, SimpleGraph.Walk.cons hadj q' => by\n    dsimp [SimpleGraph.Walk.length]\n    exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G q'.length v _ _ (mem_ballWithin_of_walk_to v q') hadj.symm\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G p.length v := by\n  have h := mem_ballWithin_of_walk_to G v p.reverse\n  rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_reverse] at h\n  exact h\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\n\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.wwbf9z/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/77001943-b7df-4df1-ba5c-db7288bf8e72/.system_generated/tasks/task-831.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user