{"step_index":847,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:28:40Z","thinking":"**Connecting `ballWithin` to `dist`**\n\nA key result demonstrates that any walk from vertex `v` to `w` implies `w` belongs to `ballWithin(G, p.length, v)`. Now, the goal is to establish a connection between `ballWithin` and the graph distance function `dist`. Exploring relevant lemmas in Mathlib, specifically `Reachable.exists_walk_length_eq_dist`, seems promising.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\\n    GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v ⊆ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\\n  exact Finset.subset_union_left\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_mono {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (v : V) {k m : ℕ} (h : k ≤ m) : GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v ⊆ GraphCalc.ballWithin G m v := by\\n  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le h\\n  induction d with\\n  | zero => exact Finset.Subset.refl _\\n  | succ d' ih =>\\n    exact Finset.Subset.trans ih (ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + d') v)\\nEOF\\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\\n\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"20000","toolAction":"\"Testing ballWithin_mono\"","toolSummary":"\"Test ballWithin_mono in scratch.lean\""}}]}
{"step_index":848,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:28:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:28:44+02:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: 77001943-b7df-4df1-ba5c-db7288bf8e72/task-848\nTask Description: cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\n\nlemma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v ⊆ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n  exact Finset.subset_union_left\n\nlemma ballWithin_mono {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (v : V) {k m : ℕ} (h : k ≤ m) : GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v ⊆ GraphCalc.ballWithin G m v := by\n  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le h\n  induction d with\n  | zero => exact Finset.Subset.refl _\n  | succ d' ih =>\n    exact Finset.Subset.trans ih (ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + d') v)\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\n\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.wwbf9z/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/77001943-b7df-4df1-ba5c-db7288bf8e72/.system_generated/tasks/task-848.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
